{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-8130"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Community Landscape Care and Maintenance Operations"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "8130"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :commercial/landscape-care-maintenance
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :water-stewardship :green-space-access]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :landscape-care-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :labor]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies [:optimization]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "`:landscape-care-governor` is implemented end-to-end in `src/landscapecare`
 as a LANDSCAPE-CARE OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor -- Landscape Care Advisor
 (LLM proposal-only, deterministic mock advisor for demo/tests) ⊣ Landscape
 Care Governor (closed-op-allowlist / site-contract-registration-before-
 any-action hard-gate / applicator-license-equipment-calibration-restricted-
 entry-interval-wind-speed-buffer-zone hard-gates, evaluated only for
 chemical-application service types / equipment-safety-clearance hard-gate,
 evaluated only for service types that require it / unresolved-safety-
 concern hard-gate / equipment-safety-clearance-or-pesticide-application-
 decision permanent block, both a structural boolean-flag check and a
 defense-in-depth text scan). Every one of its four proposal ops
 (`:log-service-record` / `:schedule-maintenance-operation` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-supply-order`) carries `:effect
 :propose` ONLY -- the governor HARD-holds any proposal that doesn't
 (`effect-not-propose-violations`). Service types split into non-chemical
 (mowing, tree-trimming/pruning -- which carries its own equipment-safety-
 clearance requirement for chainsaw/pole-saw operation, irrigation-zone
 monitoring) and chemical-application (herbicide/pesticide, with a genuine
 restricted-entry interval, maximum safe wind speed, and minimum buffer
 zone) -- the Governor's chemical-specific checks are skipped entirely,
 never fabricated, for non-chemical service types, and the equipment-
 safety-clearance check is skipped entirely for service types that do not
 require it. `:flag-safety-concern` always escalates to a human, at every
 phase, regardless of advisor confidence; `:coordinate-supply-order` above
 a cost threshold likewise always escalates; `:log-service-record` (the one
 real actuation event this actor performs) always escalates too. The
 scope-exclusion checks are deliberately phrased as the FINALIZATION
 action (e.g. \"finalize the pesticide-application decision\"), never as a
 bare noun (e.g. \"pesticide\") -- a dedicated regression test
 (`landscapecare.advisor-test`) asserts the advisor's own default mock
 proposals for every op in the closed allowlist never self-trip either
 scope-exclusion check. This build ships NO JVM-only interop anywhere in
 `src/` (all source is `.cljc`) per this workspace's cljs-first runtime-
 priority rule. See `README.md` for the full governor-check enumeration."}
